        "original_id": "5cb8df27-5c73-52ca-b7a5-ad5dd36ecdae",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: MGM Grand fire, Winecoff Hotel fire, Dupont Plaza Hotel fire\n- Places: Paradise, Nevada, Las Vegas, Atlanta, San Juan, Puerto Rico, United States\n- Buildings: MGM Grand Hotel and Casino, Bally's Las Vegas, Winecoff Hotel\n\nFacts:\n- The Winecoff Hotel fire occurred on December 7, 1946, and it killed 119 hotel occupants, including the hotel's owners.\n- The Winecoff Hotel fire was the deadliest hotel fire in United States history.\n- The MGM Grand fire occurred on November 21, 1980, at the MGM Grand Hotel and Casino, now Bally's Las Vegas, in Paradise, Nevada, USA.\n- The MGM Grand fire remains the worst disaster in Nevada history.\n- The MGM Grand fire is the third-worst hotel fire in modern U.S. history, after the 1946 Winecoff Hotel fire in Atlanta and the December 31, 1986 Dupont Plaza Hotel fire in San Juan, Puerto Rico, in which 97 people died.",
